  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Translate the lesson into explicit state and permissive logic: Each valid pallet event contributes to the selected count and produces a valid count result.",
      "Inputs are simulator feedback (pallet_detected, pallet_type_valid, count_request); PLC logic owns pallet_count_valid and the DINT pallet_count.",
      "Test the initial state, the valid condition, and at least one missing permissive.",
      "The DINT pallet_count is published after each counter scan. Stop clears the output image to zero while batch_count memory is retained; Run republishes that count, and Reset clears both."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Require the documented inputs: pallet_detected, pallet_type_valid, count_request.",
        "Publish the DINT pallet_count and command pallet_count_valid after five valid events.",
        "Remove PLC commands when the permissive is lost."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Each valid pallet event contributes to the selected count and produces a valid count result."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "pallet load",
      "pallet-type sensor",
      "count display"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "A reusable block counts manually validated pallet detection edges and publishes the current count and batch validity.",
      "startConditions": [
        "Use the built-in offline controller with the matching Demo 4 logic loaded and no active forces.",
        "Run the app scan, press machine RESET, then press machine START with PALLET off before enabling TYPE OK and COUNT REQ."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Enable pallet type valid and count request.",
        "Press NEW PALLET once for each valid event. The momentary simulation creates one rising detection edge, then releases automatically; the DINT count and 3D display advance once.",
        "The batch-valid lamp turns on at five valid events. Invalid events are not counted; held detection does not recount."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Stop clears PLC-owned BOOL and numeric outputs; the visible count becomes zero while internal counter memory is retained.",
        "Run republishes the retained counter on its next scan; a held detector does not add an event.",
        "Reset clears inputs, counter memory and outputs."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "NEW PALLET events are rejected while TYPE OK or COUNT REQ is off; each momentary press can contribute at most one count.",
        "These are manual training inputs. The optical fixture does not classify pallets or create detector transitions."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "The 3D readout and DINT pallet_count match the accumulated valid detection events. The batch-valid bit requires at least five events and both permissives.",
        "Stop clears the numeric output image to zero while retaining internal counter memory. Run republishes the retained count on its next scan. Reset clears inputs, memory and outputs.",
        "Pallet type is a manually supplied validity bit; the optical fixture does not classify pallets or generate detection events."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Five qualified NEW PALLET momentary events produce COUNT 5 and pallet_count_valid ON; RESET followed by a fresh qualified event starts batch two at COUNT 1."
    },
